{#
    The one page shell.

    Every route renders through this: the accent bar, the centred column and
    the footer are here once rather than in each template. A page that needs a
    different column width or a different accent overrides the block instead
    of restating the whole document.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="h-full bg-canvas text-ink-bright {% block html_classes %}{% endblock %}">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    {#
        Search and share metadata.

        Every value here is a block, so a page overrides the one it cares about
        and inherits the rest. `og:` and `twitter:` re-render those same blocks
        rather than restating them — there is one description per page, not
        three that drift apart.

        `|raw` on the re-rendered blocks is not a hole. `block()` returns
        output that Twig has *already* escaped once, including the quotes, so
        printing it again would double-escape an ampersand in a blader's name.
        The value is attribute-safe by the time it gets here.

        The canonical URL is built from `site_url` and the path, never from the
        request's own scheme and host. Cloudflare terminates TLS and speaks
        plain HTTP to the origin, so a request-derived canonical would tell
        Google every page lives at http:// — a second, duplicate site.

        It defaults to the path with the query string dropped, which is right
        for the pages that have no meaningful parameters and wrong for the ones
        scoped by `?season=`. Those override the block. So do the pages reached
        by more than one route: `/seasons/{slug}` and `/preseason` are the
        leaderboard again and `/v2` is the homepage again, and each says so
        here rather than letting Google pick a winner.
    #}
    <title>{% block title %}Malta Beyblade Community League{% endblock %}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="{% block description %}Standings, tournament results and blader records from Malta's Beyblade X league.{% endblock %}">
    <meta name="robots" content="{% block robots %}index, follow{% endblock %}">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{% block canonical %}{{ site_url }}{{ app.request.pathInfo }}{% endblock %}">

    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Malta Beyblade Community League">
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_MT">
    <meta property="og:title" content="{{ block('title')|raw }}">
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ block('description')|raw }}">
    <meta property="og:url" content="{{ block('canonical')|raw }}">

    {# `summary` rather than `summary_large_image`: there is no og:image yet,
       and a large-image card with no image renders worse than a small one. #}
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">

    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{ asset('favicon.svg') }}">

    {% block stylesheets %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('styles/app.css') }}">
    {% endblock %}

    {% block javascripts %}{{ importmap('app') }}{% endblock %}
</head>
<body class="min-h-full font-sans antialiased selection:bg-brand-strong selection:text-canvas {% block body_classes %}{% endblock %}">

{% block accent_bar %}
    <div class="h-2 bg-linear-to-r from-brand-strong via-flame-strong to-heat-strong"></div>
{% endblock %}

<main class="mx-auto w-full {% block column %}max-w-5xl px-3 py-12 sm:px-4 md:py-20{% endblock %}">

    {% block body %}{% endblock %}

    {{ include('_footer.html.twig') }}

</main>

</body>
</html>
